<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

    <!--
        The papillon maturation (archive/CASTES-PLAN.md §7). Two lines, both read by
        Source/Insects/PapillonMaturation.cs: how much mana the grub has spent towards pupating, and
        the cocoon's own countdown while she is inside it.
    -->

    <!-- The grub's own line. It was hidden at first (user's call, 2026-10-02) and restored the next
         day, once it was clear what the absence costs: this is a sixty-day wait at the shipping
         numbers, and a player watching a grub cannot tell a slow pupation from one that will never
         happen. -->
    <PMM_PapillonCharges>Mana spent: {0} of {1}</PMM_PapillonCharges>

    <!-- The cocoon's countdown. This key is the prefix only: the unit is one of vanilla's own period
         keys ("3 days", "18 hours", "1 hour"), which the code picks once the days run out, and that
         is where the singular comes from - a second key of ours would read "1 days". -->
    <PMM_CocoonEmergesIn>Emerges in {0}</PMM_CocoonEmergesIn>

</LanguageData>
